/**
 * hermes-farsi — DOM-level Persian localization plugin for the Hermes
 * Agent dashboard.
 *
 * Unlike a source patch, this runs against whatever build the user has
 * installed: it walks rendered text nodes and swaps known English UI
 * strings for their Persian equivalent (the dictionary below was
 * generated from a full source-level translation, so it tracks real
 * Hermes copy rather than a hand-guessed list), flips the page to RTL,
 * and loads the Vazirmatn font via style.css (see manifest.json).
 *
 * Trade-off vs. a source patch: only strings that appear verbatim in
 * the dictionary get translated. Text mixed with dynamic values (e.g.
 * "5 messages ago") won't match and stays in English. That's expected —
 * this plugin optimizes for zero-rebuild install, not 100% coverage.
 */
